    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22bbf4c8_b2ae40ad",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 399,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-23T15:41:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This patch prevents pKVM itself from setting a definitely incorrect value in the VMCS. [*] It doesn\u0027t try to impose any limitations on behavior of pvmfw itself, on the size of pvmfw image etc. (Quite the opposite, I think we try to keep the number of pKVM\u0027s requirements to a pvmfw implementation at an absolute minimum. For now, AFAICT, we have only two following requirements: 1. entry point is at the beginning of pvmfw image. 2. pvmfw starts in 32-bit mode with paging disabled, with flat 4G segments, and doesn\u0027t reload segment registers before it sets up its own GDT.)\n\nFor example, the pvmfw entry point may be at 4G-4 but its first instruction may be a jump to an earlier instruction, so it will work fine. :) Who we are to forbid a pvmfw implementation to do such strange things?\n\n[*] That said, HW guarantees that this incorrect value will result in a VM-entry failure. So I think this patch is basically optional. I can remove it if it causes confusion.",
      "parentUuid": "74ca6d6b_69680d2a",
      "revId": "a0715e9b40988b7ff0366f713c0923760105d27c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1928dbec_9de5835f",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 399,
      "author": {
        "id": 3484945
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-24T14:52:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I personally prefer to check a bit more than too less but I get your point. I would vote to add this check to guarantee that pvmfw is useful and will extend it to 3 requirements:\n- entry point is at the beginning of pvmfw image\n- pvmfw starts in 32-bit mode with paging disabled\n- taking into account above this means that first instruction must enable 64-bit to function properly and as we are quite sure that code enabling 64-bit mode will not fit in first 4B we are quite sure that such pvmfw will not be functional, right?\n\nBut I will not insist on that - if your really think it is better to leave it as is lets close this comment.",
      "parentUuid": "22bbf4c8_b2ae40ad",
      "revId": "a0715e9b40988b7ff0366f713c0923760105d27c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
